Portal sample-local CPU inference
=================================

This module is sample application code, not part of the Portal tunneling SDK.
It links llama.cpp and ggml statically into the sample's CPU-only native library.
No upstream source tree, native binary, or model weights are vendored here.

Pinned upstream release: llama.cpp v0.8.0
Release: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/tag/v0.8.0
Commit: 8642541b255bfb5dc39cd351a178be09013a55d6
Source: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/tree/8642541b255bfb5dc39cd351a178be09013a55d6
Archive: https://codeload.github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/tar.gz/8642541b255bfb5dc39cd351a178be09013a55d6
Archive SHA-256: 1688a167a8edd9499cdd0c19b8bd044f0fa184b466981977bbf2222d884953a4
Upstream C API: include/llama.h
Inference example: examples/simple/simple.cpp (llama_batch_ext / llama_process)
Original license: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/8642541b255bfb5dc39cd351a178be09013a55d6/LICENSE

Build from the repository root:
  ./scripts/build-sample-llm.sh desktop
  ./scripts/build-sample-llm.sh ios
Android uses this directory's CMakeLists.txt through externalNativeBuild with
NDK 29.0.14206865, API 26+, c++_shared, arm64-v8a/x86_64. ELF max/common page
alignment is 16 KiB. Desktop requires CMake >=3.22, C++17 and JDK17. iOS requires
Xcode, targets iOS16+, and packages static arm64 device and arm64/x86_64 simulator
libraries with the PortalSampleLlm C module and automatic c++ linkage.

Configure-time source fetching checks the pinned archive SHA-256 before
extraction and uses ~/.cache/portal-sample-llm (or XDG_CACHE_HOME/LOCALAPPDATA).
PORTAL_SAMPLE_LLM_CACHE may select a different cache outside the repository.
Build output stays under build/sample-llm; no build step downloads any model.
Model downloads are a separate, explicit application action. Model licenses and
sources are listed in samples/shared/common/models.json, independently of the
engine's MIT license. Keep this notice with redistributed sample native binaries.

Native ownership and limits:
  Each handle owns its model, 1024-token context, batch, and sampling chain.
  Requests use the model's actual chat template with a system and one user turn.
  The sampler uses top-k40, top-p0.95, temperature0.8 and distribution sampling.
  Context/sampler state resets around every request; no conversation is retained
  as inference history. Requested output is 1..128 tokens, at most four CPU
  threads. Over-budget/invalid input fails rather than being silently truncated.
  Cancel is permanent and interrupts CPU evaluation. Destroy cancels and waits
  before freeing state; do not reuse a destroyed handle. Output/error buffers
  must be freed through PortalSampleLlmFree. JNI passes standard UTF-8 byte
  arrays; generated incomplete trailing UTF-8 scalars are removed at a token cap.
  Upstream logging is disabled so model metadata, prompts, paths and answers do
  not enter application logs. The backend registry initializes once per process
  and remains resident; models and per-owner inference buffers do not.

